@startuml RPC_Sequence_Flow

title RPC (Remote Procedure Call) - How It Works

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 13

actor "Client App\n(Caller)" as Client
participant "Client Stub\n(auto-generated)" as ClientStub
participant "Network" as Network
participant "Server Stub\n(auto-generated)" as ServerStub
participant "Server App\n(Real Method)" as Server

Client -> ClientStub : Call method(params)\n(looks like local call)
ClientStub -> ClientStub : Serialize / Marshal data
ClientStub -> Network : Send encoded request

Network -> ServerStub : Deliver request
ServerStub -> ServerStub : Deserialize data
ServerStub -> Server : Invoke real method

Server -> Server : Process request
Server --> ServerStub : Return result

ServerStub -> ServerStub : Serialize response
ServerStub --> Network : Send encoded response

Network --> ClientStub : Deliver response
ClientStub -> ClientStub : Deserialize response
ClientStub --> Client : Return value\n(looks like local return)

note over Client, Server
  Defined once via Interface Description
  Language (IDL) -> generates both stubs.
  Client and Server remain fully decoupled.
end note

@enduml
